====================================================
OBJECTIVE
====================================================

Implement a permission-aware Knowledge Base editing workflow.

The goal is to support secure collaboration where document owners have full edit rights while other users can only submit suggested changes for review.

====================================================
ROLES
====================================================

Support existing roles where available.

Primary permissions:

Document Owner
- Can edit article directly.
- Can publish.
- Can approve/reject suggestions.
- Can delete own drafts.
- Can view suggestion history.

Contributor / Other User
- Cannot edit published content directly.
- Can create suggested edits.
- Can submit changes for review.
- Can view status of their suggestions.

Reviewer (if existing)
- Can review suggestions.
- Can comment.
- Can approve/reject if permitted.

====================================================
WORKFLOW
====================================================

Owner creates article
        ↓
Article published
        ↓
Another user wants to modify it
        ↓
User clicks "Suggest Changes"
        ↓
Suggested draft created
        ↓
Owner receives notification
        ↓
Owner reviews differences
        ↓
Approve
or
Reject
or
Request Changes
        ↓
If approved
Merge suggestion into article
        ↓
Create audit entry
        ↓
Update KB version

